package concept

electric_field: {
  content: #"""
    An *electric field* describes the electric influence of charges throughout
    the space around them. We can describe the field at a point by asking what
    force a small positive test charge would experience there.

    The field is present whether or not a test charge is placed at that point.
    The test charge is a way to define and measure the field; it should be
    small enough not to noticeably disturb the charges producing it.

    An electric field has both a strength and a direction. Its direction at a
    point is the direction of the force on a positive test charge there.
  """#
  related: [
    "concept/electric-field-strength",
    "law/coulomb-law"
  ]
}
